{"created": "2026-09-18T20:48:03.546793+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-18T20:48:04.044519+00:00", "id": 22837370, "conceptrecid": "22837369", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22837370", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22837369", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22837370", "metadata": {"title": "The Architecture Is Old. The Computational Actor Is New.", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22837370", "publication_date": "2026-09-13", "description": "<p>Inspired by Mike Reznikov&rsquo;s Designing RTL with C++HDL, this paper revisits the history of executable C/C++ RTL, HDL generation, and cross-domain checking. Its central hypothesis is that AI coding agents inside a fast edit&ndash;compile&ndash;test loop could change the economics of an established architectural pattern by increasing trustworthy correction and design-space search per unit cost. SystemVerilog remains the downstream compatibility and verification boundary. Proposed experiments test semantic equivalence, compare against a strong SystemVerilog plus Verilator baseline, separate representation from native-execution effects, examine downstream power, performance, and area, and distinguish migration from maintenance. The paper defines a falsifiable research program and bounded adoption test, rather than claiming an experimentally established advantage for C++HDL.</p>\n<p>Originally published September 13, 2026 at <a href=\"https://bradpierce.wordpress.com/2026/09/13/the-architecture-is-old-the-computational-actor-is-new/\">this WordPress page</a>. This Zenodo deposit preserves the published PDF unchanged.</p>\n<p>Brad Pierce supplied the originating questions, professional context, intended audience, judgments about attribution and scope, and final editorial authority. An AI language model materially assisted with research, synthesis, argument development, drafting, source checking, diagrams, adversarial and target-reader review, and document design. Brad approved the publication. The collaboration does not imply endorsement by any organization. The paper was inspired by Mike Reznikov&rsquo;s work; this acknowledgment does not make him a coauthor.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pierce, Brad", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0009-7427-2969"}], "keywords": ["C++HDL", "RTL design", "AI coding agents", "SystemVerilog", "Verilator", "executable RTL", "formal verification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://bradpierce.wordpress.com/2026/09/13/the-architecture-is-old-the-computational-actor-is-new/", "relation": "isDescribedBy", "resource_type": "publication-other", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://bradpierce.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/designing-rtl-with-chdl.pdf", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/mirekez/cpphdl", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://bradpierce.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/the-architecture-is-old-the-computational-actor-is-new.pdf"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22837369"}}]}}, "title": "The Architecture Is Old. The Computational Actor Is New.", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22837370", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22837370", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22837370?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22837370", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22837370", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22837370", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22837370/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22837369", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22837369", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22837